    responsibilities: ["Reporting organizationally to the Head of Recruiting, the Recruitment Manager will play a critical and high-impact role in driving large-scale workforce hiring and operational readiness for This major tournament. This is an extremely high-volume and high-intensity position — not a traditional recruitment role — requiring exceptional organization, resilience, and the ability to manage multiple complex projects simultaneously.","The Recruitment Manager will not only facilitate full-cycle recruitment but also lead and execute various workforce-related initiatives that involve filling hundreds of positions across multiple workforce types, each with unique processes, systems, and compliance requirements. This role demands strong project management capabilities, meticulous attention to detail, and the ability to maintain accuracy and efficiency while operating under significant pressure and evolving deadlines.","We are seeking self-starters and proactive leaders who can navigate challenges, adapt quickly, and push critical objectives to completion on time. The ideal candidate will thrive in ambiguity, possess strong leadership and problem-solving skills, and demonstrate the ability to build, refine, and scale processes to meet the operational needs of a global event.","This is a dynamic, hands-on role that requires balancing high-volume recruitment with strategic workforce execution — managing competing priorities, coordinating across functions, and ensuring delivery excellence for one of the largest sporting events in history.","This will be a 6-month temporary contract role.","The main responsibilities and oversights of the Recruitment Specialist for This major tournament include:","Lead end-to-end recruitment processes, from initial talent sourcing and screening to selection and offer negotiation, ensuring a seamless experience for both candidates and hiring managers.","Must be comfortable with a high-volume requisition load (150-250 roles at a time)."],
    qualifications: ["ACCOUNTABILITY: Demonstrate commitment to responsibilities and objectively analyze one’s behavior, while assuming consequences of one’s own actions and/or decisions and learning from one’s mistakes. DECISION MAKING: Ability to identify and swiftly make decisions in critical situations, take initiative and calculated risks, explore alternative solutions, and respond promptly to unforeseen circumstances. INCLUSIVITY: Achieve shared organizational objectives by sharing information with colleagues across all levels and divisions, tangibly influencing others, and maintaining a network of support contacts. INITIATIVE: Capacity to do things on one’s own initiative and to influence the course of events, assume responsibilities, and achieve objectives with a minimum of supervision and control. INNOVATION: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas. LEADERSHIP: Ability to lead one’s contacts/colleagues/partners, encourage teamwork, and delegate authority / decision-making power, as needed, to produce the expected results and make efficient use of the team’s skills and talents. VISION: Ability to perceive the organization's global environmental impact, anticipate decision consequences, grasp organizational missions, and formulate strategic plans. Education & Qualifications","Bachelor’s Degree (or equivalent) in Human Resources, or related field preferred. Work Experience","Minimum of 5-7 years of experience in a Talent Acquisition or HR/Workforce function.","Strong organizational and analytical skills.","Deep knowledge of modern CRM, Applicant Tracking Systems, and technologies used to attract, nurture and manage a pipeline of talent.","Demonstrated ability to project manage, prioritize effectively, manage deadlines, and work independently.","Ability to provide examples where excellent client service skills and the capacity to facilitate the needs of multiple business units has served you well in your career to date.","Demonstrated ability to drive projects forward with minimal oversight, requiring a self‑motivated and self‑directed approach to work."],
