    responsibilities: ["Reporting organisationally to the Airport manager, the Deputy Manager will be a key member of the Matchday Workforce Operational Services team and will work in close collaboration with the Transport team and other key individuals responsible for supporting the Airport Manager in overseeing all day-to-day airport operations, ensuring safety, efficiency, and compliance with aviation regulations and client service levels. This role acts as a second-in-command, providing leadership across multiple functional areas, including airside and landside operations, terminal management, customer service, and emergency response coordination.","The main responsibilities and oversights of the Deputy Airport Manager for This major tournament include:","Support and deputize for the Arrivals & Departures Teams Manager, ensuring continuity of leadership and operational decision-making.","Lead, train, and motivate a diverse team of paid staff and volunteers to deliver exceptional airport services in line with major tournament standards.","Oversee daily and shift briefings to align team performance, ensure service consistency, and address operational challenges during extended hours.","Manage all operational aspects of arrivals and departures, ensuring alignment with governance structures and coordination with airport stakeholders.","Develop and maintain effective relationships with airlines, airport authorities, transport providers, and functional areas to facilitate seamless client movements.","Direct service planning and delivery for all constituent groups, ensuring compliance with defined service levels (DSLAs) and tournament objectives."],
