    description: "Join the Matchday Workforce team delivering large-scale soccer events across North America.",
    responsibilities: ["This role is designated as match day–only and includes participation in a select number of required training sessions scheduled ahead of the tournament. Reporting organizationally to the Sustainability & Human Rights Venue Manager, the Safeguarding & Anti-Discrimination Stadium Manager (SAM) will be assigned to a specific event Venue (Stadium) to assist with delivery of safeguarding, anti-discrimination and inclusion activities on all matchdays at this stadium during the tournament.","This role will act as the consistent central point of contact and be responsible for venue specific implementation of safeguarding, anti-discrimination and inclusion matters on match days in line with the strategy, policy and procedures at the event to ensure a safe football experience for everyone.","The main responsibilities of the SAM at each venue, for the event include:","Serve as the lead contact for safeguarding and anti-discrimination inclusion matters across the designated stadium across all match days.","On matchdays, support a small group of Volunteers in performing duties designated by the Sustainability and Human Rights Venue Manager and report back on all activities at the end of shift.","On Match Day, liaise with stadium security, fan operations, CARE Team, SVM and SHR central team to respond and assist with resolution of issues or complaints related to anti-discrimination and safeguarding.","Provide case management reports to the Stadium SHR Venue Manager for concerns related to children or adults under the event Stadium Code of Conduct, ’s Safeguarding & Anti-discrimination Code of Conduct (Accredited Individuals) & ’s Code of Ethics. Anti-Discrimination Programme Implementation","Support venue-level implementation of the event Anti-Discrimination Policy, including:"],
    qualifications: ["ACCOUNTABILITY: Demonstrate commitment to responsibilities and objectively analyze one’s behavior, while assuming consequences of one’s own actions and/or decisions and learning from one’s mistakes. DECISION MAKING: Ability to identify and swiftly make decisions in critical situations, take initiative and calculated risks, explore alternative solutions, and respond promptly to unforeseen circumstances. INCLUSIVITY: Achieve shared organizational objectives by sharing information with colleagues across all levels and divisions, tangibly influencing others, and maintaining a network of support contacts. INITIATIVE: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas. INNOVATION: Capacity to break new ground, look for unconventional solutions, and produce fresh ideas. LEADERSHIP: Ability to lead one’s contacts/colleagues/partners, encourage teamwork, and delegate authority / decision-making power, as needed, to produce the expected results and make efficient use of the team’s skills and talents. VISION: Ability to perceive the organization's global environmental impact, anticipate decision consequences, grasp organizational missions, and formulate strategic plans. Education & Qualifications","Qualifications in safeguarding, human rights or public protection or demonstrable knowledge and practical experience in a related occupation. Work Experience","Minimum requirements:","Demonstrable practical experience in the field of security, public protection, human rights, civil rights, anti-discrimination and safeguarding.","Communication skills and experience in working in multi-cultural environments.","Knowledge on how to recognize behaviors that are discriminatory and harmful to children and adults and understanding the impact of abusive behavior;","Ability to work professionally, confidentially and consistently in an area where emotionally distressing and sensitive issues and cases may arise.","Knowledge about the Host Cities legal and socio-cultural context, government guidelines and national frameworks on anti-discrimination and safeguarding;"],
