    payLabel: "Competitive",
    payDetail: "",
    description: "Join the Matchday Workforce team delivering large-scale soccer events across North America.",
    responsibilities: ["This role provides site-level security delivery oversight for Team Base Camp venues that consist of the Hotel and Training Site that a participating national football team will occupy throughout major tournamentTM. Intended to be a home away from home, a Team Base Camp (TBC) refers to a team’s headquarters where they stay and perform necessary functions to compete at This major tournamentTM.","Reporting organizationally to the Safety and Security Senior Manager – Non-Competition Sites, the Team Base Camp Specialist acts as the primary on-site security representative at Team Base Camps during tournament time.","The role focuses on site readiness, private security supervision, and operational assurance, ensuring that security services are delivered in accordance with approved standards, post orders, contractual obligations, and operational directives. Site Readiness & Operational Assurance","Ensure assigned Team Base Camp sites are operationally ready for security delivery prior to and throughout tournament operations","Verify that private security personnel are correctly briefed, trained, and deployed in accordance with their assigned duties and post orders","Confirm that security infrastructure and equipment (access control points, barriers, CCTV, lighting, radios, signage, etc.) are installed (where applicable), functional, and appropriately configured","Conduct readiness checks and daily operational verifications at assigned Team Base Camp sites","Validate that access control arrangements and security zoning are implemented as approved"],
    qualifications: ["Education & Qualifications: •\tBachelor's degree in a related field associated with safety, security and/or project management is a plus","All candidates must be able to pass a comprehensive background check","Must be available for duration of the Team’s residence","Must be willing to work long hours and be on call 24/7 during the tournament. Work Experience:","Minimum 3–5 years of experience in security operations, preferably in major events, hospitality, logistics, or VIP environments","Experience supervising or coordinating private security services","Familiarity with hotel security operations and transport/logistics environments","Strong understanding of access control, incident response, and operational security principles"],
