    description: "Join the Matchday Workforce team delivering large-scale soccer events across North America. major tournament Skills Framework ACCOUNTABILITY: Demonstrate commitment to responsibilities and objectively analyze one’s behavior, while assuming consequences of one’s own actions and/or decisions and learning from one’s mistakes. DECISION MAKING: Ability to identify and swiftly make decisions in critical situations, take initiative and calculated risks, explore alternative solutions, and respond promptly to unforeseen circumstances. INCLUSIVITY: Achieve shared organizational objectives by sharing information with colleagues across all levels and…",
    responsibilities: ["The Ceremonies Production Integration role is a key position within This major tournament Events & Entertainment Team (EET), consolidating the responsibilities of Production Manager, Senior Operations Manager, Senior Show Delivery Manager, Senior Scenic & Systems Manager, Operations Manager, Site Manager, and Production Support roles across 4th of July ceremonies programs.","This role supports the full lifecycle of ceremonies – from concept development and technical/production planning, through rehearsals, live show delivery, site and back-of-house operations, and legacy handover. It ensures that all ceremonies-related production, staging, scenic, systems, site operations, and logistics are delivered on time, safely, efficiently, and in alignment with ’s creative vision, operational standards, and safety policies.","The position works in close collaboration with EET internal departments, Event Management Companies (EMCs), stadium management, Logistics, Venue Management, Broadcast, Marketing, IT, Security, Accreditation, Workforce & Volunteers, and other major tournament Functional Areas (FAs). The role also plays a central part in managing documentation, project plans, production schedules, call sheets, reports, creative assets, and operational data to support a seamless ceremony delivery.","This is a high-intensity, live-event operations role requiring strong project management, show delivery, technical understanding, stakeholder management, and the ability to adapt quickly to changing circumstances in a stadium environment. Project & Production Management","Support the development, management, and distribution of production, staging, scenic, systems, and ceremonies operational plans from concept to delivery.","Assist in the development of ceremonies deliverables, coordinating event details, internal alignment, and approval processes.","Work alongside Heads of Operations, Technical, and Resourcing to oversee technical requirements and integration of ceremonies with stadiums and show environments.","Develop and implement broadcast, staging, and scenic requirements and processes, in collaboration with EMCs and relevant Functional Areas."],
    qualifications: ["Education & Qualifications","Bachelor’s degree in Event Management, Live Entertainment Production, Theatre Production, Sports Event Management, Technical Production, or a related field preferred.","Equivalent professional experience in ceremonies, large-scale live events, or stadium show production will be considered in lieu of a degree.","Work Experience","Extensive experience working on large-scale live events, preferably in stadium environments (sporting events, ceremonies, concerts, or similar).","Demonstrated experience in event logistics and operations, working cross-functionally across large event delivery teams.","Experience with vendors and suppliers, including negotiation, coordination, and performance oversight.","Exposure to or experience with production elements such as lighting, sound, video, rigging, staging, scenic, and broadcast integration."],
